#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:1
msgid "llvm-reduce - LLVM automatic testcase reducer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-reduce` \\[*options*\\] \\[*input...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-reduce` tool project that can be used for reducing the "
"size of LLVM test cases. It works by removing redundant or unnecessary code "
"from LLVM test cases while still preserving their ability to detect bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:16
msgid ""
"If `input` is \"`-`\", {program}`llvm-reduce` reads from standard input. "
"Otherwise, it will read from the specified `filenames`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:19
msgid ""
"LLVM-Reduce is a useful tool for reducing the size and complexity of LLVM "
"test cases, making it easier to identify and debug issues in the LLVM "
"compiler infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:23
msgid "GENERIC OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:26
msgid "Display available options (--help-hidden for more)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:30
msgid "Abort if any reduction results in invalid IR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:34
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of delta passes to run. By default, {program}`llvm-"
"reduce` runs all available delta passes for the input format (IR or MIR). "
"When specified, only the listed passes will be executed, in the given order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:38
msgid ""
"Available delta passes can be listed using {option}`--print-delta-passes`. "
"Specific passes can also be excluded using {option}`--skip-delta-passes`. If "
"an unrecognized pass name is specified, {program}`llvm-reduce` will report "
"an error and exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:45
msgid ""
"WARNING: This option will replace your input file with the reduced version!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:49
msgid ""
"A textual description of the pass pipeline, same as what's passed to `opt -"
"passes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:53
msgid ""
"Maximum number of threads to use to process chunks. Set to 1 to disable "
"parallelism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:57
msgid ""
"Maximum number of times to run the full set of delta passes (default=5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:61
msgid "Set the target triple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:65
msgid ""
"Don't disable features used for crash debugging (crash reports, llvm-"
"symbolizer and core dumps)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:69
msgid ""
"Print list of delta passes, passable to {option}`--delta-passes` as a comma-"
"separated list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:73
msgid ""
"Delta passes to not run, separated by commas. By default, run all delta "
"passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:77
msgid ""
"Do not validate testcase is interesting after counting chunks. This will "
"save time by avoiding extra executions of the interestingness test, but a "
"warning will no longer be printed on flaky reproducers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:83
msgid "Number of times to divide chunks prior to first test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:85
msgid ""
"Note : Granularity refers to the level of detail at which the reduction "
"process operates. A lower granularity means that the reduction process "
"operates at a more coarse-grained level, while a higher granularity means "
"that it operates at a more fine-grained level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:91
msgid "Name of the interesting-ness test to be run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:95
msgid "Arguments passed onto the interesting-ness test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:99
msgid "Print extra debugging information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:103
msgid "Always write temporary files as bitcode instead of textual IR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:107
msgid "Input language as ir or mir."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:110
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:112
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-reduce` returns 0 under normal operation. It returns a non-"
"zero exit code if there were any errors. Returns 2 if the interestingness "
"test reported the initial input was not interesting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:116
msgid "EXAMPLE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:118
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-reduce` can be used to simplify a test that causes a compiler "
"crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:121
msgid ""
"For example, let's assume that `opt` is crashing on the IR file `test.ll` "
"with error message `Assertion failed at line 1234 of WhateverFile.cpp`, when "
"running at `-O2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:125
msgid ""
"The test case of `test.ll` can be reduced by invoking the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:132
msgid "The shell script passed to the option `test` consists of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:140
msgid ""
"(In this script, `grep` exits with 0 if it finds the string and that becomes "
"the whole script's status.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-reduce.md:143
msgid ""
"This example can be generalized to other tools that process IR files, for "
"example `llc`."
msgstr ""
